  "id": "USN-9079-1",
  "summary": "nfdump vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that nfdump incorrectly handled certain input files,\nleading to a buffer overflow. If a user or automated system were tricked\ninto processing a specially crafted file, an attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause nfdump to crash or execute arbitrary code.\n(CVE-2019-1010057)\n\nIt was discovered that nfdump incorrectly handled certain IPFIX template\nwithdrawal messages, leading to an integer overflow. A remote attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause nfdump to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2019-14459)",
